  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kazakhstan Rule of Law Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Kazakhstan):  The Kazakhstan Rule of Law activity (KROL) strengthens the independence of the judiciary and creates a favorable legal environment for businesses and civil society organizations (CSOs). The objectives of the activity include: (1) strengthening the investment climate and business enabling environment, (2) improving the legal enabling environment for nonprofit organizations and (3) increasing independence and professionalism of the judiciary.  The program&apos;s focus on implementation of the newly adopted Administrative Procedure and Process Code was designed to allow businesses and investors to understand that the Courts could serve as a check on agency decisions that were otherwise unpredictable and lacked the appearance of impartiality. USAID will support improvements to the administrative procedural code by introducing presumption of innocence best practices. Partnering with the Union of Judges, the activity plans to improve the Judicial Code of Ethics. The activity also plans to work with the Ministry of Information and Social Development to create a new Law on Non-Commercial Organizations and provide online courses for legislation drafting to align this process with international standards to make the lawmaking process more transparent and participatory. USAID will support efforts to build the Government-CSOs partnership to further promote transparency and accountability.This activity contributes to the U.S.Integrated Country Strategy Objective 2.2: Democratic institutions and human rights protections are enhanced by advancing civil liberties and rule of law, and demonstrating political will to conduct objective, transparent investigations into allegations of official misconduct;  and U.S. Strategy for Central Asia Objective 5: Promote rule of law reform and respect for human rights and Objective 6: Promote US investment in and development of Central Asia;  CAATSA Goal 2: Anti-corruption and rule of law and Goal 5: independent media and civil society.</narrative>
  </description>
